1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,808
Bump your elbow and ZAP!

2
00:00:01,808 --> 00:00:04,730
A weird electric tingle shoots down your arm.

3
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:08,574
The twist: your “funny bone” isn't a bone at all.

4
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:12,209
It's your ulnar nerve.

5
00:00:12,209 --> 00:00:15,985
At the elbow it sits in a shallow groove, under just skin and fat.

6
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:22,195
A bump squeezes the nerve against the bone, and it fires off a burst of signals.

7
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,434
Your brain feels it where that nerve goes: the ring and little fingers.

8
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:30,996
Why “funny”?

9
00:00:30,996 --> 00:00:34,538
One theory: a pun on humerus, the arm bone, and humorous.

10
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,952
The zing fades within minutes.

11
00:00:38,952 --> 00:00:42,377
If those fingers often stay numb or tingle, see a doctor.
